---
import BaseLayout from "@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="AI use - Joacim Eldre"
  description="How and why I use generative artificial intelligence to make a small part of this website."
>
  <section>
    <div class="pt-16">
    <h1 class="typo-display-xl">
        How I use AI on this website.
    </h1>
    <p class="mt-4 typo-main">
        I've used generative artificial intelligence to help me create the stackable decagon in the footer, for the latest Bluesky post integration that fetches the latest post from my Bluesky profile, for the tag system used in posts, and for the clap API to Redis integration.
    </p>
    <h2 class="mt-8 mb-4 typo-display-lg">
        How this website indirectly uses AI.
    </h2>
    <p class="mt-4 typo-main">
        I honestly have no idea, and that's problematic. I think GitHub, Vercel, and Astro all use generative artificial intelligence in their products. I'll dig and update this to be as open as possible.
    </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
